    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #284\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-223-inbox-pipeline-04-07-fingerprint-inbox-thr_ypm9swju35` (the branch backing PR #284).\n\nNote: the remote had moved ahead (a `develop` merge had been pushed to this branch in the meantime, bringing in unrelated Gmail-watch-lifecycle work), so I merged that in locally (clean, no conflicts) before pushing, rather than force-pushing over it.\n\nThis push includes the fix for the medium-severity finding from the latest review: `findExistingProposal` now scans all `sourceInbox` edges instead of trusting `edges[0]`, so it correctly finds the live proposal even when a soft-deleted proposal's edge coexists with its live replacement's — preventing unbounded proposal creation on repeated ticks. A regression test covers this two-edge scenario.\n\nVerified post-merge: `tsc --noEmit` clean, full suite passes (22 files, 281 tests, 0 failures).\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
